# Cluster Reconnaissance & Network Discovery

Hands-on training drill covering cluster architecture inspection, network topology extraction, Pod CIDRs, Service
CIDR discovery, and API resource taxonomy.

## Official Exam References & Quick Lookups

### Permitted Exam Documentation

- **Cluster Networking**: [Cluster Networking](https://kubernetes.io/docs/concepts/cluster-administration/networking/) `[EXAM ALLOWED]`
- **Kubernetes API Overview**: [API Overview](https://kubernetes.io/docs/concepts/overview/kubernetes-api/) `[EXAM ALLOWED]`

### In-Exam Search Keywords

- `"cluster networking"`
- `"service-cluster-ip-range"`
- `"podCIDR"`
- `"api-resources"`

### Terminal Fast Lookups (`kubectl` & Host Inspection)

```bash
# Extract assigned Pod CIDR per node:
kubectl get nodes -o custom-columns=NODE:.metadata.name,POD_CIDR:.spec.podCIDR

# Discover Service CIDR from apiserver manifest:
grep -E -- "--service-cluster-ip-range" /etc/kubernetes/manifests/kube-apiserver.yaml

# Inspect CNI plugin network configuration:
ls -la /etc/cni/net.d/

# Count namespaced vs non-namespaced API resources:
kubectl api-resources --namespaced=true
kubectl api-resources --namespaced=false
```

